Time Complexity:

Let n = length of string s

    Traversing string s → O(n)
    Traversing string t → O(n)

Overall: O(n)


Space Complexity:

    Only constant variables used

Overall: O(1)


Approach:

1. Initialize:
   - asciiSumS = 0
   - asciiSumT = 0

2. Traverse string s:
   - Add ASCII value of each character to asciiSumS

3. Traverse string t:
   - Add ASCII value of each character to asciiSumT

4. Compute difference:
   - asciiSumT - asciiSumS

5. The difference represents ASCII value of extra character

6. Typecast result to char and return it




class Solution {
    public char findTheDifference(String s, String t) {
        int asciiSumS= 0;
        int asciiSumT= 0;
        for(int i=0; i<s.length(); i++){
            asciiSumS += s.charAt(i);
        }
        for(int i=0; i<t.length(); i++){
            asciiSumT += t.charAt(i);
        }
        return (char)(asciiSumT - asciiSumS);
    }
}
